          <td>
            <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#FFFFFF" size="2">In 
              the conflict between the good and evil races, Edge of Infinity holds 
              a neutral standpoint. Edge of Infinity accepts recruits from all 
              races and classes. </font></p>
            <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#FFFFFF" size="2">The 
              members in Edge of Infinity are expected to be honorable in their 
              actions towards other members and people outside of the guild. Incidents 
              concerning members will be taken in a case by case matter, if a 
              punishment is neccisary it will be fair and just. </font></p>
            <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#FFFFFF" size="2">Edge 
              of Infinity is not a heavy role playing guild, the members here 
              are just here to have some fun. You may roleplay in Norrath if you 
              wish, or you may decide not to roleplay. As long as your decision 
              does not hinder the decisions of others. </font></p>
            <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#FFFFFF" size="2">As 
              the guild leader, I feel that I do not like the idea of making it 
              difficult to join a guild. Because of this I feel that having officer 
              status is not a large issue. When someone is promoted to officer, 
              that person does not have any more responsibility than the standard 
              member. The only responsibility that person has is to actively recruit 
              members. If that person feels that they would like someone in the 
              guild and they are of the appropriate level, 30+, then they are 
              welcome to invite that person. Being an officer of the guild means 
              that you wish to help make the guild prosper.</font></p>
            <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#FFFFFF" size="2"> 
              Guild decisions will generaly be made by me, I will listen to the 
              opinion of guild members. Generally the decisions I make will be 
              from a neutral standpoint, and will depend on the feedback I get 
              from guild members. There will be some instances in which a sudden 
              and immediate action may be required, such as members who show conduct 
              that stains the reputation of the guild. </font></p>
            <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#FFFFFF" size="2"><b><font size="3" color="#0000CC">Guild 
              Raids:</font></b></font></p>
            <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#FFFFFF" size="2">First 
              of all when I speak about this section, it pertains ONLY to big 
              guild raids that have been planned, and not common guild groups.</font></p>
            <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#FFFFFF" size="2"> 
              Items that are obtained from guild raids are to be randomed first 
              by need. If nobody in the group within the dungeon can use the item, 
              anyone in the guild who is at that dungeon may random for the item 
              provided they need and can use the item. If all else fails the item 
              can be randomed within the group that found the item to be sold 
              for coin.</font></p>
            <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#FFFFFF" size="2"> 
              Items that are obtained from a guild group are suggested to go with 
              the Need before Greed rule. However I do not feel the need to impose 
              restrictions on the way that a group from the guild functions. </font></p>
            <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#FFFFFF" size="2"><b><font size="3" color="#0000FF">Item 
              Camping:</font><font size="3"> </font></b></font></p>
            <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#FFFFFF" size="2">When 
              a member is in need of assistance that person may ask help from 
              the guild. He/she may then post on the message boards that that 
              person is going to camp an item and is asking for assistance from 
              the members. That person is responsible for organizing the item 
              camp with the members. Everyone that goes to the item camp goes 
              in with the knowledge that the specific item they are going for 
              goes to the person who asked for and organized the item camp, any 
              other items that happen to be obtained will be randomed by the group 
              according to Need before Greed.</font></p>
            <p>&nbsp;</p>
            <p align="right"><i><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" size="2">Jedaka, 
              Guild Leader, 07 May 2000</font></i></p>
